WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:04.670
Avengers: Endgame's relatively light body
count surprised a lot of fans.

00:00:04.670 --> 00:00:08.440
Shocked by its predecessor's carnage, audiences
braced themselves for loss.

00:00:08.750 --> 00:00:13.120
Thankfully, the majority of Earth's heroes
survived the latest encounter with Thanos,

00:00:13.120 --> 00:00:15.400
which raises a new question: why?

00:00:15.840 --> 00:00:18.340
It doesn't really seem like there's one right
answer.

00:00:18.920 --> 00:00:22.860
Endgame gave us a ton of heroes, and the filmmakers
likely had different reasons for keeping each

00:00:22.880 --> 00:00:25.160
survivor off the chopping block.

00:00:25.660 --> 00:00:28.360
Here's why we think the following Avengers
survived Endgame.

00:00:28.760 --> 00:00:33.380
Everyone's favorite trash panda came out of
Avengers: Endgame relatively unscathed.

00:00:33.760 --> 00:00:37.660
The easiest and most likely answer to the
question of Rocket's survival is Guardians

00:00:37.660 --> 00:00:39.160
of the Galaxy Volume 3.

00:00:39.820 --> 00:00:46.379
At Hasbro HASCON 2017, Guardians writer/director
James Gunn told fans he had an origin story

00:00:46.380 --> 00:00:47.920
for Rocket that he planned to tell.

00:00:48.580 --> 00:00:52.800
He also warned Rocket' s life story would
likely be more "horrible" than it was in the

00:00:52.800 --> 00:00:53.300
source material.

00:00:53.660 --> 00:00:59.870
By March 2019, Gunn was confirmed as directing
the movie using his screenplay, so all things

00:00:59.870 --> 00:01:03.469
considered, it looks like we might be learning
more about Rocket's past in Guardians of the

00:01:03.469 --> 00:01:04.500
Galaxy Volume 3.

00:01:05.140 --> 00:01:09.540
It would be a pretty big bummer if we only
got to see that story after Thanos turned

00:01:09.540 --> 00:01:10.360
him into a small rug.

00:01:10.860 --> 00:01:14.220
Unfortunately we didn't see a lot of Okoye
in Avengers: Endgame.

00:01:14.900 --> 00:01:18.760
She's in the final battle and briefly speaks
to Black Widow in the beginning of the film.

00:01:19.240 --> 00:01:20.300
Beyond that, she's absent.

00:01:20.840 --> 00:01:25.360
Fortunately, that also seemed to increase
her overall chances of surviving through the

00:01:25.360 --> 00:01:26.100
movie's end.

00:01:26.580 --> 00:01:31.120
In Infinity War, T'Challa's last interaction
with Okoye is pretty memorable:

00:01:31.700 --> 00:01:32.399
"Up.

00:01:32.400 --> 00:01:33.800
This is no place to die."

00:01:38.120 --> 00:01:41.720
In a way, this moment is also the answer to
her survival in Endgame.

00:01:41.900 --> 00:01:46.820
Okoye is part of the MCU as a whole, but she's
particularly important to the Black Panther

00:01:46.820 --> 00:01:47.460
franchise.

00:01:47.849 --> 00:01:52.279
If she were to ever make the ultimate sacrifice,
it should be in a Black Panther film.

00:01:52.280 --> 00:01:56.840
Not only that, but the aftermath of Infinity
War and Endgame leaves us with a lot of questions

00:01:56.880 --> 00:02:01.220
about Wakanda and we're probably going to
need Okoye to get some of those answers.

00:02:01.980 --> 00:02:05.739
After all, while the people who were snapped
were brought back to life, they still did

00:02:05.740 --> 00:02:09.780
disappear, which means T'Challa was effectively
dead for five years.

00:02:10.440 --> 00:02:14.140
The king of Wakanda died without an heir and
his sister Shuri was dead as well.

00:02:14.900 --> 00:02:16.960
What happened in Wakanda during those five
years?

00:02:17.380 --> 00:02:19.180
Who is T'Challa going to find on the throne?

00:02:19.580 --> 00:02:23.500
Valkyrie was one of the most asked-about absences
from Avengers: Infinity War.

00:02:24.060 --> 00:02:28.120
Along with Korg and Miek, we never see her
during Thanos' attack on the Asgardian refugee

00:02:28.120 --> 00:02:31.240
ship and we didn't know if she'd survived
the purge.

00:02:31.880 --> 00:02:36.540
Avengers: Endgame finally gives us our answers:
Along with the rest of the surviving Asgardians,

00:02:36.540 --> 00:02:38.520
Valkyrie settles in New Asgard.

00:02:39.140 --> 00:02:43.879
With Thor wallowing in depression, alcohol,
and Fortnite when Avengers: Endgame begins,

00:02:43.880 --> 00:02:45.080
someone has to take charge.

00:02:45.730 --> 00:02:50.320
So the once-apathetic warrior we meet in Thor:
Ragnarok, who once only cared about kidnapping

00:02:50.320 --> 00:02:54.080
refugees and drinking...becomes the de facto
Queen of New Asgard.

00:02:54.820 --> 00:02:59.739
Her contributions don't stop at the administrative;
she also flies in on a winged horse in the

00:02:59.740 --> 00:03:01.080
final battle against Thanos.

00:03:01.880 --> 00:03:03.500
Valkyrie's star is rising.

00:03:03.980 --> 00:03:07.800
Considering Marvel's statements about increasing
diversity in its films, and the fact that

00:03:07.800 --> 00:03:12.500
Valkyrie is a bisexual woman of color, not
to mention that regardless of her sexuality

00:03:12.500 --> 00:03:18.040
or ethnicity she was a hugely popular part
of Ragnarok, the character has massive potential

00:03:18.040 --> 00:03:20.260
in the post-Endgame MCU.

00:03:21.040 --> 00:03:23.080
Killing her off so early would be a huge waste.

00:03:23.920 --> 00:03:28.700
Captain Marvel's ticket sales broke many records,
and continue to break more, and there's definitely

00:03:28.700 --> 00:03:33.439
going to be a sequel, so the idea of killing
her off in Avengers: Endgame would have been

00:03:33.440 --> 00:03:34.040
pretty nuts.

00:03:34.469 --> 00:03:39.099
Beyond Captain Marvel's own franchise, Avengers:
Endgame opens an opportunity for the hero

00:03:39.100 --> 00:03:41.020
to perform another role: leader.

00:03:41.820 --> 00:03:46.720
Endgame left a huge void in the Avengers'
leadership; Captain America is now eligible

00:03:46.720 --> 00:03:49.660
to join AARP, and Black Widow and Iron Man
are dead.

00:03:49.660 --> 00:03:54.120
If the Avengers are going to move forward
they'll need a new leader, and those are shoes

00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:56.800
the Carol Danvers has filled in the comics.

00:03:57.360 --> 00:03:59.680
We're pretty certain the big screen version
could do the same.

00:04:00.080 --> 00:04:03.320
Thor was another hero a lot of fans guessed
was going to get the axe.

00:04:03.940 --> 00:04:08.120
His entire family is dead, his hammer got
shattered, his people are practically extinct,

00:04:08.120 --> 00:04:09.639
and his home exploded.

00:04:09.900 --> 00:04:11.639
"We can rebuild this place.

00:04:11.640 --> 00:04:16.940
It will become a haven for all peoples and
aliens of the universe."

00:04:19.610 --> 00:04:23.020
Why wouldn't the thunder god make another
suicide run at Thanos?

00:04:23.020 --> 00:04:24.020
What does he have left to live for?

00:04:24.220 --> 00:04:26.020
Well, for one thing, better movies.

00:04:26.660 --> 00:04:31.580
Taika Waititi's Thor: Ragnarok revived the
whole Thor franchise, before that, Chris Hemsworth

00:04:31.580 --> 00:04:33.400
had apparently grown bored with the character.

00:04:34.120 --> 00:04:37.700
But now the sky's the limit, which is exactly
where Thor is headed.

00:04:38.100 --> 00:04:42.139
He hops aboard the Benatar toward the end
of Endgame to join the Guardians of the Galaxy,

00:04:42.140 --> 00:04:46.060
so does this mean we should expect Thor to
be a part of the Guardians of the Galaxy Vol.

00:04:46.060 --> 00:04:46.560
3?

00:04:47.040 --> 00:04:50.560
Or is what he said to Valkyrie true; are the
Guardians just giving him "a ride," maybe

00:04:50.760 --> 00:04:52.340
to another Waititi-directed Thor film?

00:04:52.480 --> 00:04:56.720
Or is this the last time we should expect
to see the Odinson outside the comics?

00:04:57.280 --> 00:04:59.400
We don't know, and Hemsworth says he doesn't
either.

00:05:00.080 --> 00:05:03.340
Regardless, the potential is there, and that's
enough to keep him alive.

00:05:03.960 --> 00:05:04.460
"Cool?

00:05:04.720 --> 00:05:05.220
Cool."

00:05:05.380 --> 00:05:05.880
"So cool."

00:05:06.320 --> 00:05:10.320
Rhodey was pretty much right at the top of
the list of characters most people expected

00:05:10.320 --> 00:05:11.660
to die in Endgame.

00:05:12.340 --> 00:05:12.940
He's a sidekick.

00:05:13.200 --> 00:05:15.700
He had a shot at a solo film that never materialized.

00:05:16.200 --> 00:05:19.520
His superhero name is one of the least family-friendly
titles you could think of.

00:05:20.080 --> 00:05:22.920
"War Machine was a little too aggressive,
alright, this sends a better message."

00:05:22.980 --> 00:05:27.180
And to top it all off, Thanos did kill him
in the comics, and not that long ago.

00:05:27.380 --> 00:05:32.580
During an ill-fated assault on the Mad Titan
in 2016's Civil War II, Thanos put his fist

00:05:32.580 --> 00:05:34.200
through War Machine's chest.

00:05:34.480 --> 00:05:38.360
If you're not a comics reader but you saw
Endgame with friends who are Marvel Comics

00:05:39.080 --> 00:05:43.020
fans, you can bet they were worried when Thanos
headed for Morag while Rhodey and Nebula were

00:05:43.020 --> 00:05:44.460
there trying to get the Power Stone.

00:05:44.660 --> 00:05:48.280
All of that is precisely why Rhodey survives
Endgame.

00:05:48.420 --> 00:05:52.160
During the span of the four films they've
directed for Marvel Studios, Joe and Anthony

00:05:52.160 --> 00:05:55.340
Russo have proven their mastery at going against
expectation.

00:05:55.980 --> 00:05:59.420
They're not going to kill Rhodey when everyone
is thinking they're going to kill Rhodey.

00:06:00.080 --> 00:06:03.540
Considering what we've seen from them, they
probably put Rhodey on the Morag team because

00:06:03.540 --> 00:06:08.160
they knew fans would be seeing skulls as soon
as Thanos set course for the rock.

00:06:08.780 --> 00:06:11.960
Nebula's survival was one of the most surprising
outcomes of Endgame.

00:06:12.580 --> 00:06:16.860
She has a "hack first, think later" attitude
that never serves her well against her powerful

00:06:16.860 --> 00:06:17.360
father.

00:06:17.900 --> 00:06:20.940
She's impulsive, damaged, and suffers a well
of endless rage.

00:06:20.940 --> 00:06:23.720
"I thought you were the biggest sadist in
the galaxy."

00:06:24.180 --> 00:06:25.940
"That was when daddy was paying my bills."

00:06:25.940 --> 00:06:30.240
In Guardians of the Galaxy Vol. 2 she flies
a spaceship into a cavern while trying to

00:06:30.340 --> 00:06:33.800
kill Gamora, and she keeps going even after
the wings break off.

00:06:34.240 --> 00:06:38.060
If there's one thing the Hulk teaches us in
the opening scene of Infinity War, it's that

00:06:38.060 --> 00:06:42.140
your head better pack as much of a punch as
your fists if you're going after Thanos.

00:06:42.640 --> 00:06:45.200
All in all, Nebula seemed doomed from the
start.

00:06:45.800 --> 00:06:47.260
But she survives Endgame.

00:06:47.480 --> 00:06:51.520
At least, the Nebula of the present survives,
her past self gets a hole in her chest.

00:06:52.340 --> 00:06:56.800
One of the reasons Nebula survives is likely
the same as Rhodey; the expectation of death

00:06:56.800 --> 00:06:59.560
was high, so the Russo brothers went in the
opposite direction.

00:07:00.250 --> 00:07:05.020
But probably the biggest reason is her potential
in Guardians of the Galaxy Vol. 3.

00:07:05.030 --> 00:07:09.610
On one hand, if Nebula were to die in Endgame,
then Mantis would be the only woman left on

00:07:09.610 --> 00:07:12.979
the team, since the whereabouts of 2014 Gamora
are unknown.

00:07:12.980 --> 00:07:16.560
On the other, Endgame changes Nebula dramatically.

00:07:17.169 --> 00:07:19.680
She's spent years with the Avengers and with
Rocket.

00:07:19.680 --> 00:07:21.560
She's played paper football with Tony Stark.

00:07:21.960 --> 00:07:26.500
The Nebula we meet in Vol. 3 will be a very
different cyborg than the one we're used to.

00:07:27.300 --> 00:07:31.440
Marvel's Green Goliath was expected to be
headed to the gladiator arena in the sky after

00:07:31.440 --> 00:07:36.160
the story broke that Mark Ruffalo filmed five
different endings to Avengers: Endgame.

00:07:37.060 --> 00:07:41.070
Once the much more articulate version of the
Hulk slid on the new Infinity Gauntlet, it's

00:07:41.070 --> 00:07:44.800
likely fans were worried this was going to
be the end for the Jade Giant.

00:07:45.260 --> 00:07:46.480
But it wasn't meant to be.

00:07:46.800 --> 00:07:51.110
He gets a nasty burn on his arm, and the last
time we see him he's still wearing a sling,

00:07:51.110 --> 00:07:53.980
but Bruce Banner gets to live to see the aftermath
of Endgame.

00:07:54.590 --> 00:07:58.800
One possible reason for the Hulk's continued
existence might be found in the most recent

00:07:58.800 --> 00:08:01.820
rumor about Disney+'s MCU original series.

00:08:02.520 --> 00:08:07.500
While nothing's been confirmed, shortly before
Endgame's release a report circulated that

00:08:07.500 --> 00:08:11.540
a Hulk and She-Hulk series was in development
for the upcoming streaming service.

00:08:12.420 --> 00:08:16.490
In the comics, it's Bruce Banner's cousin
who becomes She-Hulk after he's forced to

00:08:16.490 --> 00:08:18.220
save her life with a blood transfusion.

00:08:18.700 --> 00:08:23.120
Whether those details will remain the same,
or if the series is actually in development,

00:08:23.120 --> 00:08:23.640
remains a mystery.

00:08:24.200 --> 00:08:28.400
But it could prove to be the reason the MCU
Hulk survived saving half the people in the

00:08:28.400 --> 00:08:28.900
universe.

00:08:29.620 --> 00:08:31.620
Things look really bad for Cap in Endgame.

00:08:32.300 --> 00:08:35.840
Once Thanos starts shredding his shield with
that huge double sword, it seems like he's

00:08:35.840 --> 00:08:39.950
finally going to get to visit Peggy Carter
and the Howling Commandos in the U.S.O. show

00:08:39.950 --> 00:08:40.950
in the sky.

00:08:40.950 --> 00:08:46.190
Now, Chris Evans' contract is up and if there's
an unwritten code of comic book laws somewhere,

00:08:46.190 --> 00:08:49.280
one of those rules is that when Cap's shield
breaks, all bets are off.

00:08:50.120 --> 00:08:54.360
Thankfully for Cap, Peggy, and all of us,
Steve is still with us, though he's a bit

00:08:54.360 --> 00:08:54.900
older.

00:08:55.320 --> 00:08:59.500
Once the big, final battle is over, Cap uses
his assignment to return the Infinity Stones

00:08:59.500 --> 00:09:04.840
to their rightful places in the timeline to
also return to the love of his life, Peggy.

00:09:05.520 --> 00:09:10.680
An aged Steve Rogers hands off his shield
to Sam Wilson, and so ends the saga of the

00:09:10.680 --> 00:09:12.510
MCU's original Captain America.

00:09:12.510 --> 00:09:15.400
It's almost unthinkable to end Cap's journey
any other way.

00:09:15.940 --> 00:09:19.720
To simply kill him, even in some glorious,
heroic manner, isn't enough.

00:09:20.460 --> 00:09:24.800
Just as Tony Stark deserves his rest, Steve
Rogers deserves the chance to live a full

00:09:24.810 --> 00:09:27.420
life and finally get that dance with Peggy.

00:09:27.420 --> 00:09:27.940
"Figured I'd wait."

00:09:29.020 --> 00:09:29.560
"For what?"

00:09:31.620 --> 00:09:32.320
"The right partner."

00:09:32.760 --> 00:09:37.710
And with two other founding MCU Avengers dying
in Endgame, we needed at least one to get

00:09:37.710 --> 00:09:38.220
a happier ending.

00:09:38.920 --> 00:09:43.450
The only thing Hawkeye does better than shoot
arrows is fool audiences about who's going

00:09:43.450 --> 00:09:43.980
to die.

00:09:44.450 --> 00:09:49.120
In a 2016 interview, Aaron Taylor-Johnson,
who played Quicksilver in Avengers: Age of

00:09:49.120 --> 00:09:54.170
Ultron, said that one of the reasons his character
dies saving Hawkeye is that director Joss

00:09:54.170 --> 00:09:58.210
Whedon was playing with the widespread belief
that Hawkeye would die in the sequel.

00:09:58.210 --> 00:10:02.080
Directors Joe and Anthony Russo seemed to
use a similar strategy for Avengers: Endgame.

00:10:02.080 --> 00:10:06.900
Hawkeye and Black Widow are tasked with getting
the Soul Stone, meaning one of them must sacrifice

00:10:07.080 --> 00:10:07.940
themselves for it.

00:10:08.440 --> 00:10:10.160
Hawkeye seems the perfect choice.

00:10:10.720 --> 00:10:14.660
With his despair about the horrific things
he's done since the purge, he barely seems

00:10:14.660 --> 00:10:16.140
like a candidate for a happy ending.

00:10:16.600 --> 00:10:18.980
Instead it's Black Widow who dies for the
Stone.

00:10:19.320 --> 00:10:22.060
Hawkeye also survives because he has more
work to do.

00:10:22.640 --> 00:10:27.840
In early April 2019, Variety reported that
a series featuring Hawkeye was in development

00:10:27.840 --> 00:10:30.400
for the upcoming Disney+ streaming service.

00:10:30.400 --> 00:10:32.060
That's likely not the biggest reason, though.

00:10:32.780 --> 00:10:37.260
After all, Black Widow has an upcoming film,
and neither Vision nor Loki receive Endgame

00:10:37.480 --> 00:10:40.740
resurrections despite similar upcoming Disney+
series.

00:10:41.120 --> 00:10:44.040
Perhaps the chief reason Hawkeye survives
is his family.

00:10:44.940 --> 00:10:49.080
For his wife and children to be resurrected
at the end without Clint to welcome them,

00:10:49.080 --> 00:10:51.660
would be too tragic a note for a story already
rife with grief.

00:10:52.850 --> 00:10:56.500
Spider-Man's death scene = Avengers: Infinity
War was one of the most gut-wrenching in a

00:10:56.500 --> 00:10:58.100
sequence filled with death scenes.

00:10:58.370 --> 00:10:59.720
"I don't wanna go.

00:10:59.720 --> 00:11:00.600
I don't wanna go, sir.

00:11:00.600 --> 00:11:01.140
Please."

00:11:01.240 --> 00:11:05.960
Surprising no one, he returns after the Hulk
uses the Infinity Stones to reverse Thanos'

00:11:05.960 --> 00:11:06.500
purge.

00:11:07.060 --> 00:11:11.360
He's a major player in the final battle against
Thanos and his forces, being one of the Avengers

00:11:11.360 --> 00:11:16.141
to secure the Infinity Gauntlet from the Mad
Titan until he inevitably gets it back, but

00:11:16.141 --> 00:11:17.240
loses all the same.

00:11:18.020 --> 00:11:22.120
Of course, the fact that we all saw the Spider-Man:
Far from Home trailer months before the release

00:11:22.180 --> 00:11:26.500
of Endgame was a big hint that Peter would
not only come back, but survive the film.

00:11:27.040 --> 00:11:31.760
To anyone who wasn't sure the purged heroes
of Infinity War would return, T'Challa's death

00:11:31.760 --> 00:11:33.600
was one that should have convinced them.

00:11:34.240 --> 00:11:38.540
With Black Panther proving to be one of Marvel
Studios' most successful films, the first

00:11:38.540 --> 00:11:43.110
superhero film to be nominated for a Best
Picture Oscar, and writer/director Ryan Coogler

00:11:43.110 --> 00:11:48.080
already working on a sequel, it was obvious
the King of Wakanda couldn't stay dead forever.

00:11:48.500 --> 00:11:52.500
Which isn't to say his death in Infinity War
is meaningless or without stakes.

00:11:53.340 --> 00:11:57.900
In spite of his resurrection, by the time
Black Panther 2 hits the screen, Wakanda will

00:11:57.900 --> 00:12:00.440
have gone at least five years without its
king.

00:12:00.700 --> 00:12:05.940
Not only that, but T'Challa is lost at a crucial
time in the nation's history when, at T'Challa's

00:12:06.040 --> 00:12:10.780
direction, it moves away from isolationism
and reveals its technological superiority

00:12:10.780 --> 00:12:11.360
to the world.

00:12:12.080 --> 00:12:17.680
We don't know who, if anyone, was on the throne
in T'Challa's absence, Ramonda, maybe M'Biaku.

00:12:18.460 --> 00:12:22.491
The nation he returns to in Black Panther
2 will likely be very different from the one

00:12:22.500 --> 00:12:24.420
he died fighting for in Infinity War.

00:12:25.120 --> 00:12:28.760
People were not happy with Doctor Strange
after Avengers: Infinity War.

00:12:29.360 --> 00:12:34.200
In spite of Strange telling Tony that surrendering
the Time Stone to Thanos was "the only way,"

00:12:34.200 --> 00:12:38.220
once he gets back to Earth, Stark accuses
Strange of quote, "giving away the stone."

00:12:38.380 --> 00:12:42.150
Bruce Banner doesn't seem very happy with
Strange either when he tells the Ancient One

00:12:42.150 --> 00:12:42.980
about what he did.

00:12:43.400 --> 00:12:48.440
Of course, in the end it turns out that the
one timeline in which Thanos loses needs Tony

00:12:48.440 --> 00:12:49.220
Stark alive.

00:12:49.540 --> 00:12:53.700
The fact remains that Strange did give up
the Eye of Agamotto, which means the forces

00:12:53.700 --> 00:12:55.920
of Kamar-taj have lost their greatest weapon.

00:12:56.640 --> 00:13:01.000
Thanos destroys all of the Infinity Stones
before Thor kills him, but even after some

00:13:01.000 --> 00:13:05.360
time travel hijinks that return all the Stones
from the past to their respective times and

00:13:05.660 --> 00:13:09.980
places so that nothing is disrupted, the Time
Stone will still be destroyed.

00:13:10.340 --> 00:13:14.350
The relic that allowed Strange to outwit Dormammu
[door-MAH-moo] is gone, and Kamar-taj needs

00:13:14.350 --> 00:13:15.860
Doctor Strange more than ever.

00:13:16.260 --> 00:13:19.980
Of course, none of that would matter if there
weren't going to be any more Doctor Strange

00:13:19.980 --> 00:13:21.480
films, but on that score we don't need to
worry.

00:13:22.380 --> 00:13:27.060
In December 2018, The Hollywood Reporter broke
the news that Doctor Strange director Scott

00:13:27.060 --> 00:13:31.720
Derrickson was poised to return for the sequel,
and Cumberbatch seems just as eager to return

00:13:31.720 --> 00:13:32.360
to his Sanctum.

00:13:32.720 --> 00:13:36.050
The end of Endgame proves to be a new beginning
for Sam Wilson.

00:13:36.420 --> 00:13:41.560
While the Avengers expect Captain America
to return from his time jaunt as planned,

00:13:41.560 --> 00:13:45.840
instead an aged Steve Rogers appears, wearing
a wedding ring and waiting for Falcon so he

00:13:45.840 --> 00:13:48.260
can pass on a heavy burden to the much younger
hero.

00:13:48.800 --> 00:13:53.180
Sam Wilson is poised to be the new Captain
America, as he was for a time in the comics.

00:13:53.180 --> 00:13:57.920
He seems reluctant to accept the shield at
first; when Steve asks how the shield feels,

00:13:57.920 --> 00:14:00.220
Sam says "Like it's someone else's."

00:14:00.810 --> 00:14:05.780
Once Steve responds "It isn't," Sam takes
a long, deep breath and thanks his old partner.

00:14:05.780 --> 00:14:09.960
On one hand, Falcon's death would be problematic
considering he and Bucky are about to share

00:14:09.960 --> 00:14:11.400
a miniseries on Disney+.

00:14:11.920 --> 00:14:16.620
More importantly, Falcon can't die because
the legacy of Captain America needs to live

00:14:16.620 --> 00:14:20.080
on in younger hands, and for many reasons
it couldn't be Bucky.

00:14:20.880 --> 00:14:24.040
Forget Black Widow, that guy's got way too
much red in his ledger.

00:14:24.600 --> 00:14:28.820
Before seeing Endgame, you could hardly blame
anyone for putting Bucky in their Avengers:

00:14:28.820 --> 00:14:29.820
Endgame death pool.

00:14:30.240 --> 00:14:35.460
He isn't exactly the most popular superhero,
and considering the blood-soaked past he wrestles

00:14:35.460 --> 00:14:40.240
with, it's easy to imagine the former HYDRA
assassin would see death as a welcome respite.

00:14:40.240 --> 00:14:44.440
The Winter Soldier's most predictable role
post-Endgame would have been as the new Captain

00:14:44.440 --> 00:14:49.170
America, considering Chris Evans' MCU exit
and the fact that Bucky took up the mantle

00:14:49.170 --> 00:14:54.170
of Captain America for a time in the comics,
but we now know that honor went to Sam Wilson.

00:14:54.170 --> 00:14:57.830
The Falcon's going to need some guidance in
his new role, and as much as he and Bucky

00:14:57.830 --> 00:15:02.630
haven't gotten along in the past, Bucky's
probably the best choice for Sam's partner.

00:15:02.630 --> 00:15:06.360
Speaking with Entertainment Weekly, the Russo
brothers confirmed that Bucky knew about Cap's

00:15:06.360 --> 00:15:11.240
plan to go back in time to get back the life
he lost when he plunged into the ice.

00:15:11.240 --> 00:15:15.780
Considering Bucky seems unsurprised by Cap
handing the shield over to Sam, it seems likely

00:15:15.800 --> 00:15:17.900
the two also discussed what needed to happen.

00:15:18.320 --> 00:15:22.080
We're probably going to see what that help
looks like in the upcoming Disney+ Falcon/Winter

00:15:22.080 --> 00:15:23.080
Soldier series.

00:15:23.760 --> 00:15:24.980
"You couldn't have done that earlier?"

00:15:26.420 --> 00:15:26.940
"I hate you."

